      playstore
      nodejs is phone
      express is an app
      mongodb is another app
      npm installs them

step 3:
  create project folder
    mkdir assetflow

step 4:
   npm init -y
      it creates package.json(id card of your project)

step 5:
    why do we need express?
       node js requires much more code
       express provides a simpler way
          create api
          handle routes
          receive requests
          send response
          use middleware

        think:
          node->engine
          express ->car built on that engine

step 6:
   install express
       npm ->connects to npm registry->downloads express-> downloads express dependencies
       ->stores them in node_modules -> updates package.json-> update package-lock.json
    what is node_modules:
        node_modules->express->body parser -> cookie -> debug -> mime ->etc..
    why we do not upload node_modules to github?
        npm install because anyone recreate it by running so we ignore it using .gitignore
