    project structure
      server
      client
      
      cd server
         again initialize node for backend
         npm init -y
         npm install express mongoose dotenv bcrypt jsonwebtoken cors
         
day 2:
 step 1:
   create index.js:
     why: when you start npm start how does node know which file to run
         answer it looks package.json
            {
                "name":"server"
                "version":"1.0.0"
                "main":"index.js"
            }
            like main()in c or java
  step 2:
     const express=require("express"); =>to load the express library into this file
     const app=express() =>your application (manager everything goes through it)
         app.get(),app.post(),app.use(),app.listen()
      const port=5000 they talk to a specific port not talk to your computer
          localhose:3000 react
          localhost:5000 backend
      app.listen(port,()=>{

      }) start the server and wait for incomint requests.
    get http method
    "/" url path
    req => keep the browser info
    res => keep the server sent info


node.js =>js
mongodb=>bson

translator is mongoose
      mongoose is a library that helps node.js communicate with mongodb

odm is object document mapper
   object:
     const user={name:"sudha"} js
   document:
     { "name":"sudha"} mongodb
    mapper: mongoose (converts data mongo to js or viceversa)
why dotenv:
   database password should never be written directly in code
       mongoose.connect("mongodb+srv//admin12345@cluster...")
             everyone see your password
       use :
         .env:
            mongouri=...
       now code use like "process.env.mongouri

config folder:
   professional projects keep configuration separate.
    we will have:
      mongodb,jwt,cloudinary,email,redis
